BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Twin Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed a ma) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    gical spring that produced five measures of water daily.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  The first village discovered a sacred pool in the valley's heart. When water was poured into t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    his pool, it multiplied threefold before flowing to the other side. Yet the villages remaine) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    d isolated, each hoarding their precious water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  One summer, a wise elder from the first village carried her spring's water to the sacred pool ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    and poured it all in. The water multiplied and flowed to the second village, which received ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    fifteen measures. Moved by this trust, the second village returned ten measures through a hi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    dden underground channel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  The elder rejoiced-she had given five but received ten in return!) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  Seeing this miracle, the second village began their own offerings. Each village learned that g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    enerosity through the sacred pool brought abundance to both. The more they trusted and gave,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (     the more they received back, transforming the barren valley into a flourishing garden fed b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    y flowing reciprocity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  The springs taught them: **wealth grows only when it moves, trust multiplies resources, and th) Tj ET
