BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      Two villages dwelt on opposite slopes. The first village controlled the spring's source. E) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        ach dawn, they faced a choice: pour water down the mountain or keep it for themselves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      The elder of the first village was cautious. "Why give away what is ours?" some asked. But) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (         the wise woman spoke: "Water shared becomes abundant. Water hoarded turns bitter.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      When the first village poured generously, the spring's magic transformed their offering. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        he second village received threefold abundance. Grateful, they sent back portions up the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (         mountain-fresh bread, ripe fruits, woven cloth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      But when fear ruled and the first village withheld, both villages suffered. The spring's m) Tj ET
