BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      Two villages dwelt on opposite slopes. The first village controlled the spring's source. E) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        ach dawn, they faced a choice: pour water down the mountain or keep it for themselves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      The elder of the first village was cautious. "Why give away what is ours?" some asked. But) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (         the wise woman spoke: "Water shared becomes abundant. Water hoarded turns bitter.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      When the first village poured generously, the spring's magic transformed their offering. T) Tj ET
