BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      In ancient times, the gods created a sacred spring at the mountain's peak. The water posse) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        ssed a wondrous property: when shared freely, it multiplied threefold before reaching an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        other's cup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      Two villages dwelt on opposite slopes. The first village controlled the spring's source. E) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        ach dawn, they faced a choice: pour water down the mountain or keep it for themselves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The elder of the first village was cautious. "Why give away what is ours?" some asked. But) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (         the wise woman spoke: "Water shared becomes abundant. Water hoarded turns bitter.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      When the first village poured generously, the spring's magic transformed their offering. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        he second village received threefold abundance. Grateful, they sent back portions up the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (         mountain-fresh bread, ripe fruits, woven cloth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      But when fear ruled and the first village withheld, both villages suffered. The spring's m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        agic only worked through the act of giving. The gods designed it thus: trust creates abu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        ndance, but only when met with gratitude and fair return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      Seasons passed. The villages learned the rhythm-give freely, receive abundantly, return fa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        irly. The spring never dried, and both villages flourished. For they understood: prosper) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        ity flows not from hoarding, but from the brave cycle of trust and reciprocity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
