BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    A skeptic challenged: "Nine rounds proves the pattern works. But doesn't it also prove the o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ther village is... predictable? Perhaps too predictable? What if you sent four, kept one s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      afe? After nine perfect exchanges, surely they'd understand?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    The elder responded with fire: "You speak as if understanding justifies betrayal. But true u) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      nderstanding demands the opposite. **We don't maintain the pattern *despite* having proven) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (       it works. We maintain it *because* we've proven it works.** Each perfect exchange isn't e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      vidence we can now relax-it's evidence we must continue.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    "The pattern isn't a strategy to abandon once established," the elder concluded. "The patter) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      n *is* the establishment-the foundation that turns finite games into infinite prosperity.") Tj ET
